[
    {
        "content": "<p>What would be the general approach to proving <code>(HashSet.contains (HashSet.insert .emptyWithCapacity y) x) -&gt; x = y</code>, or <code>x ∈ {y, z} -&gt; x = y ∨ x = z</code>? Using rewrites or simps immediately leads to the<code>Internal</code> namespace, this isn't the correct approach right?</p>",
        "id": 586389429,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1776625393
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you have a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 586392093,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1776627842
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well I've mostly failed so far, but as an example proof state, if you attempt</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Hashable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">contains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emptyWithCapacity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emptyWithCapacity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">keys</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DHashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">keys</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DHashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">keys</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>you find yourself with the goal</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">DHashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Internal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">foldRev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emptyWithCapacity</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inner</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inner</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and I'm assuming we're not meant to be dealing with the <code>Internal</code> namespace, right?</p>",
        "id": 586392395,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1776628033
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would it be okay to additionally assume <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=EquivBEq#doc\">docs#EquivBEq</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LawfulHashable#doc\">docs#LawfulHashable</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 586392993,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1776628635
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Hashable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">EquivBEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LawfulHashable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LawfulBEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Added</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">contains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emptyWithCapacity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">eq_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I assume nothing will work without these assumptions</p>",
        "id": 586393155,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1776628786
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah fantastic, this is actually what I was looking for then. Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 586393269,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1776628881
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I started with</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"644391\">@loogle</span> Std.HashSet.contains, Std.HashSet.insert</p>\n<p>which found <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Std.HashSet.contains_insert#doc\">docs#Std.HashSet.contains_insert</a> and then it turned out I needed <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=beq_iff_eq#doc\">docs#beq_iff_eq</a> as well</p>",
        "id": 586393292,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1776628896
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"search\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f50d\" role=\"img\" title=\"search\">:search:</span> <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Std/Data/HashSet/Lemmas.html#Std.HashSet.contains_insert_self\">Std.HashSet.contains_insert_self</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Std/Data/HashSet/Lemmas.html#Std.HashSet.contains_insert\">Std.HashSet.contains_insert</a>, and <a href=\"https://loogle.lean-lang.org/?q=Std.HashSet.contains%2C%20Std.HashSet.insert\">2 more</a></p>",
        "id": 586393296,
        "sender_full_name": "loogle",
        "timestamp": 1776628897
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Huh, reading <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Std.HashSet.contains_insert#doc\">docs#Std.HashSet.contains_insert</a> I think that's exactly the precise lemma needed to handle all similar cases (proofs about the members of small hashsets)</p>",
        "id": 586393408,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1776629001
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I didn't notice it at first because I hadn't realized <code>==</code> is useful in this case. thanks again!</p>",
        "id": 586393529,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1776629120
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A small remark about the exact typeclass assumptions: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LawfulBEq#doc\">docs#LawfulBEq</a> implies both <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=EquivBEq#doc\">docs#EquivBEq</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LawfulHashable#doc\">docs#LawfulHashable</a>, so if you're assuming <code>LawfulBEq</code> then you can omit the other two.</p>",
        "id": 587677057,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1776663010
    }
]